[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556161585,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556208785,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556214225,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556218475,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556221945,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556225425,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556228815,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556232245,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556235845,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556239265,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556242285,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556245805,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS`, and the CI gate shards (`kaggle_run.py shards`) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556251815,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` | IBM jobs; narrow replays the CPU runs faster |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556256425,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556260145,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. Batch pushes requesting either ID ran on 4-core CPU machines without libtpu, so this account reaches no TPU through the CLI | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556264845,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556269325,"data":"| IBM Heron (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 15 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556273455,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556277545,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556281335,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556285095,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556288545,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556291985,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556295555,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556299375000002,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556302635,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556308675,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556312195,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556323235,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack. The kernel fetches the eight\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556326745,"data":"   pinned archives (sha256-checked), installs them through the PKGBUILD\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556330465,"data":"   recipes in `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`, runs `--extract`, and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556334415,"data":"   stops with exit code 3 unless the regenerated\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556338275,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json` equals the retained bytes.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556342775,"data":"   The build host passes the same test against its Arch packages, so a run\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556346475,"data":"   that reaches its entry used the same algebra code as the host.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556349565,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556353475,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556357375,"data":"4. The entry's stdout, stderr, exit code and changed files.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556361005,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556364416,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556367976,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556371316,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556374936,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556378036,"data":"| qiskit | 2.5.2 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556381645,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556385045,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556388836,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556392765,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556395876,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI (Cayley-Calculator runtime) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556398685,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556401576,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556404445,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556407176,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556410616,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556414396,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556418545,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556422756,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556426236,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556429636,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556433625,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556437285,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556446696,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556454016,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556457815999998,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556461616,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556465405,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":17.556468896,"data":"\n"}
